281
00:21:33,481 --> 00:21:36,780
Made in America isn't only about the textile and electronic

282
00:21:36,781 --> 00:21:37,780
industries.

283
00:21:37,781 --> 00:21:40,180
Our food has also reached the global market.

284
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:46,160
Discovery Foods in Hayward, California,

285
00:21:46,161 --> 00:21:49,060
has become one of the largest frozen food distributors

286
00:21:49,061 --> 00:21:49,761
in the country.

287
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:56,300
And this American company has become the top provider

288
00:21:56,301 --> 00:22:01,700
of a very popular Asian appetizer, the potsticker,

289
00:22:01,701 --> 00:22:05,240
Also known as a dumpling, the potsticker consists of a meat

290
00:22:05,241 --> 00:22:09,740
or vegetable filling thinly wrapped in dough.

291
00:22:09,741 --> 00:22:12,340
A dumpling is traditionally boiled,

292
00:22:12,341 --> 00:22:13,840
where the potsticker is fried.

293
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:19,660
Our Ling Ling potstickers are the leading parts

294
00:22:19,661 --> 00:22:21,360
to potstickers in the world.

295
00:22:21,361 --> 00:22:24,860
We have the largest market share of anyone in the United States,

296
00:22:24,861 --> 00:22:28,660
well-recognized as the authentic, great-tasting potsticker

297
00:22:28,661 --> 00:22:31,020
to give the real Asian experience

298
00:22:31,021 --> 00:22:33,060
with the convenience of home preparation.

299
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,900
This is the beginning of our process

300
00:22:37,901 --> 00:22:39,540
in our mixing and grinding room.

301
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:43,300
We process roughly 25,000 pounds of chicken a day.

302
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:52,100
10 tons of cabbage

303
00:22:52,101 --> 00:22:54,640
and enough flour in the process

304
00:22:54,641 --> 00:22:57,420
to make 15,000 loaves of bread every day.

305
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:07,780
We bring in our raw chicken, grind it, mix it with the cabbage, spices and oils.

306
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:16,560
The ingredients are finely blended together to reach a consistent filling.

307
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:24,260
At the same time, the dough ingredients are mixed, then threaded to a ribbon to flatten out the dumpling skin.

308
00:23:24,261 --> 00:23:27,260
The remaining scraps of dough are collected,

309
00:23:27,261 --> 00:23:29,260
then recycled back through the ribbon

310
00:23:29,261 --> 00:23:31,260
to create more dumpling circles,

311
00:23:31,261 --> 00:23:34,260
wasting as few grains of flour as possible.

312
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:39,260
Now it's time to create the dimpled dumplings.

313
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:45,260
The dough is cut into circles,

314
00:23:45,261 --> 00:23:49,260
and the dumplings are loaded with 12 and a half grams of filling.

315
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,260
The automated process that we use

316
00:23:51,261 --> 00:23:54,460
that we use assures uniformity of the skin

317
00:23:54,461 --> 00:23:57,100
and consistency of the filler.

318
00:23:57,101 --> 00:24:00,260
By selling the calibration of each of the machines,

319
00:24:00,261 --> 00:24:03,100
we know precisely how thick the skin is,

320
00:24:03,101 --> 00:24:05,300
how much filler is in each potsticker,

321
00:24:05,301 --> 00:24:07,580
and what the total weight of each unit is.

322
00:24:07,581 --> 00:24:12,380
Our potsticker line produces more than 25 potstickers per second,

323
00:24:12,381 --> 00:24:15,260
or over a million potstickers every day.

324
00:24:15,261 --> 00:24:25,380
They are then pinched with stainless steel fingers to mimic the look and feel of a dumpling

325
00:24:25,381 --> 00:24:34,260
that was made by hand.

326
00:24:34,261 --> 00:24:39,220
The potstickers then head to the freeze process to lock in the freshness.

327
00:24:39,221 --> 00:24:44,220
This is the spiral freezer, which preserves the products

328
00:24:44,221 --> 00:24:48,220
so that they are wholesome and great tasting for our consumers.

329
00:24:48,221 --> 00:24:50,220
In this freezer, we maintain the temperature

330
00:24:50,221 --> 00:24:52,220
at minus 14 degrees Fahrenheit.

331
00:24:52,221 --> 00:24:56,220
The product resides in here, moving up the spiral

332
00:24:56,221 --> 00:24:58,220
for a period of 23 minutes,

333
00:24:58,221 --> 00:25:00,220
at which time it is completely frozen

334
00:25:00,221 --> 00:25:03,220
and ready for our bagging and packaging operation

335
00:25:03,221 --> 00:25:05,220
to ship to our consumer.

336
00:25:05,221 --> 00:25:07,220
This American phenomenon is a great

337
00:25:07,221 --> 00:25:14,840
This American phenomenon of buy now, eat later allows highly perishable foods to be distributed

338
00:25:14,841 --> 00:25:22,820
all over the world without compromising its freshness or taste for months to come.

339
00:25:22,821 --> 00:25:28,700
The frozen food industry can be credited to New York taxidermist Clarence Birdseye, whose

340
00:25:28,701 --> 00:25:35,840
1923 quick-freeze method revolutionized food in the U.S.

341
00:25:35,841 --> 00:25:41,500
This technique works by quickly exposing foods to extremely low temperatures.

342
00:25:41,501 --> 00:25:48,300
In accelerating the freeze time, fewer ice crystals form, which can damage tissue structure.

343
00:25:48,301 --> 00:25:57,360
As a result, the fresh taste remains until the consumer is ready to eat.

344
00:25:57,361 --> 00:26:03,240
The frozen pot stickers work their way over to the weighing and packaging area.

345
00:26:03,241 --> 00:26:09,680
An elaborate system of computerized scales is used to weigh out one bag of potstickers.

346
00:26:09,681 --> 00:26:15,120
They pass through several weigh buckets in order to wean down any excess pieces.

347
00:26:15,121 --> 00:26:21,020
Once the buckets approve the weight, the potstickers are combined for a final portion calculation,

348
00:26:21,021 --> 00:26:24,000
then dropped into the bag.

349
00:26:24,001 --> 00:26:31,420
At this rate, the packaging line seals over 52,000 bags a day.

350
00:26:31,421 --> 00:26:36,560
Another million potstickers heads to stores.

351
00:26:36,561 --> 00:26:39,560
And this bubbled appetizer is ready for you

352
00:26:39,561 --> 00:26:43,140
whenever you are ready for it.

