00:27:43,301 --> 00:27:44,140
toys.

367
00:27:44,141 --> 00:27:51,840
Connex in Hatfield, Pennsylvania, is the only large-scale toy manufacturing company

368
00:27:51,841 --> 00:27:56,539
in the United States. By thinking outside of the box, this U.S.

369
00:27:56,540 --> 00:27:58,180
company now sells over

370
00:27:58,181 --> 00:28:03,988
10 million sets a year. Started in 1992 in just 500 U.S.

371
00:28:03,989 --> 00:28:07,100
retail stores, Connex toys are

372
00:28:07,101 --> 00:28:13,140
now carried in 17,000 stores in over 40 countries.

373
00:28:13,141 --> 00:28:15,040
The concept is simple.

374
00:28:15,041 --> 00:28:20,260
Take a rod and connector, snap them together, and repeat.

375
00:28:20,261 --> 00:28:26,540
These basic parts allow for an infinite amount of possibilities and have spawned a new generation

376
00:28:26,541 --> 00:28:30,820
of K'nex toys.

377
00:28:30,821 --> 00:28:37,360
The modern-day toy factory consists of an army of stainless steel, high-tech machinery.

378
00:28:37,361 --> 00:28:46,160
K'nex has over 250,000 square feet of manufacturing automation, working 24 hours a day, seven

379
00:28:46,161 --> 00:28:48,360
days a week.

380
00:28:48,361 --> 00:28:52,940
Our manufacturing process is known as plastic injection molding.

381
00:28:52,941 --> 00:28:59,540
Essentially, we're making fancy jello molds in stainless steel to exactly whatever part

382
00:28:59,541 --> 00:29:07,620
it is when a newly designed part comes in from the development team a stainless steel cavity

383
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:14,500
must be created using state-of-the-art mold fabrication precision lasers electronically

384
00:29:14,501 --> 00:29:20,660
burn out the cavity which is to mirror the design of the rod connector or brick

385
00:29:20,661 --> 00:29:27,900
Outdoor silos hold over 200,000 pounds of petroleum-based plastic

386
00:29:27,901 --> 00:29:32,680
before the material is brought in to be melted and molded into a part.

387
00:29:34,040 --> 00:29:38,500
The basic injection molding process is the taking of a solid plastic,

388
00:29:39,220 --> 00:29:42,400
feeding it up into the proportional loader, mixing it with color,

389
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:45,480
and converting it into a liquid at a very high temperature,

390
00:29:45,481 --> 00:29:50,140
in this case, 420 degrees, which will come out of the nozzle

391
00:29:50,141 --> 00:29:52,860
and shoot into the back of the tool

392
00:29:52,861 --> 00:29:56,200
and actually push the molten plastic

393
00:29:56,201 --> 00:29:58,380
into the cavities of the tool

394
00:29:58,381 --> 00:30:00,900
to form the impression of that cavity,

395
00:30:00,901 --> 00:30:03,680
which in this case is a Kinex rod.

396
00:30:08,420 --> 00:30:11,240
Each press is microprocessor controlled

397
00:30:11,241 --> 00:30:13,060
and self-diagnosed

398
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:16,200
with a clamping force of over 400 tons.

399
00:30:16,201 --> 00:30:20,200
With over 5 billion parts made each year,

400
00:30:20,201 --> 00:30:23,200
Kinex is the only major U.S. manufacturer

401
00:30:23,201 --> 00:30:26,200
able to compete with China's grip on toy production.

402
00:30:26,201 --> 00:30:31,200
The reason we're able to compete with everybody around the world with our parts

403
00:30:31,201 --> 00:30:35,200
is because we've automated and invested in incredible technology

404
00:30:35,201 --> 00:30:38,200
to get the precision of the parts every time.

405
00:30:38,201 --> 00:30:41,200
So every one of these 5 billion parts that we make every year,

406
00:30:41,201 --> 00:30:44,200
the parts are better, the parts are less expensive,

407
00:30:44,201 --> 00:30:46,960
expensive and they're closer to our customers.

408
00:30:46,961 --> 00:30:51,040
It's what Made in America is all about.

409
00:30:51,041 --> 00:30:53,240
K'nex is known for its big ideas,

410
00:30:53,241 --> 00:30:55,400
such as working grandfather clocks,

411
00:30:55,401 --> 00:30:59,260
bikes you can ride, to even a fully functional 8,000 piece

412
00:30:59,261 --> 00:31:00,500
Ferris wheel.

413
00:31:00,501 --> 00:31:04,300
It'll take a good builder anywhere from 15 to 20 hours

414
00:31:04,301 --> 00:31:05,560
to put together.

415
00:31:05,561 --> 00:31:07,440
And definitely with this many pieces,

416
00:31:07,441 --> 00:31:09,240
you can then build whatever you imagine.

417
00:31:11,960 --> 00:31:13,440
The system is infinite.

418
00:31:13,441 --> 00:31:15,100
You can really build anything you want,

419
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:18,340
but we know we just can't sell one single box of toys,

420
00:31:18,420 --> 00:31:19,780
so we do prescribed building,

421
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:23,000
whether it's a roller coaster, a car, an airplane.

422
00:31:23,420 --> 00:31:26,000
We want kids to buy multiple K'nex toys

423
00:31:26,001 --> 00:31:27,720
that can all work together.

424
00:31:27,860 --> 00:31:28,960
It's a big bin at home.

425
00:31:29,140 --> 00:31:30,560
Once you get more, you dump them in,

426
00:31:30,561 --> 00:31:33,540
and you just keep growing and growing the bin of K'nex parts

427
00:31:33,541 --> 00:31:35,040
so you can build anything you want.

428
00:31:35,500 --> 00:31:37,640
From the classics to the confusing,

429
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:41,200
no idea is too simple or perplexing

430
00:31:41,201 --> 00:31:42,900
for the development team at K'nex.

431
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:50,440
This group spends countless hours working on creating the next great toy set or model.

432
00:31:50,441 --> 00:31:55,440
The design process starts in a couple of different ways.

433
00:31:55,441 --> 00:31:58,440
We take an idea and we do what we call a sketch.

434
00:31:58,441 --> 00:32:04,440
And that sketch starts either on the computer or with the parts that we have and do a physical sketch.

435
00:32:04,441 --> 00:32:09,440
We then take that sketch and show it to the design team and the marketing team

436
00:32:09,441 --> 00:32:14,440
team and sometimes focus groups as well and see if that sketch has some legs to it.

437
00:32:14,441 --> 00:32:20,440
Once those legs are built, the toy needs to be carefully dissected and mapped out

438
00:32:20,441 --> 00:32:25,440
because the construction of the set is all part of the fun.

439
00:32:25,441 --> 00:32:31,440
Graphic designers are given the task to devise steps that pose a challenge for the assembler,

440
00:32:31,441 --> 00:32:35,440
but at the same time maintaining a user-friendly appeal.

441
00:32:35,441 --> 00:32:40,680
We spend about half of our development dollars doing the instructions so that a kid can have

442
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:42,960
guaranteed success no matter what age.

443
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:46,940
The vibrant colors have more purpose than aesthetic appeal,

444
00:32:47,740 --> 00:32:49,940
but also speak a universal language.

445
00:32:51,620 --> 00:32:55,224
It's designed so it can be used by any kid anywhere in the world.

446
00:32:55,225 --> 00:32:58,440
The color coding is important because we don't want words.

447
00:32:59,020 --> 00:33:04,440
So just color-coded building instructions lets the instruction books be clear to everybody.

448
00:33:04,441 --> 00:33:07,940
And that global reach has helped turn the toy construction set

449
00:33:08,040 --> 00:33:13,440
business into a $20 billion a year industry.

450
00:33:13,540 --> 00:33:16,320
However, this booming growth has greatly influenced

451
00:33:16,420 --> 00:33:19,820
the manufacturing community.

452
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:23,300
Toys used to be made just about 100% here.

453
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:24,920
And over the last 25 years, you've

454
00:33:25,020 --> 00:33:29,300
seen America shed about 45% of their manufacturing jobs

455
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:31,100
overseas.

456
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:33,800
But with 95% of its production happening

457
00:33:33,801 --> 00:33:36,600
in the United States.

458
00:33:36,601 --> 00:33:40,040
Connects is creating more jobs for U.S. workers.

459
00:33:40,041 --> 00:33:44,740
If we had just designed here and did everything in China,

460
00:33:44,741 --> 00:33:47,580
then we'd probably have only about 10 or 12 employees here

461
00:33:47,581 --> 00:33:49,480
instead of 200.

462
00:33:49,481 --> 00:33:52,560
And that ripple effect is about another 3,000 jobs

463
00:33:52,561 --> 00:33:54,420
in this area.

464
00:33:54,421 --> 00:33:57,020
According to the U.S. Chamber of Commerce,

465
00:33:57,021 --> 00:34:00,300
for every one manufacturing job, several more are created

466
00:34:00,301 --> 00:34:04,800
in sectors such as supply, transportation, and web design.

467
00:34:04,801 --> 00:34:07,360
We're able to have Americans helping Americans,

468
00:34:07,361 --> 00:34:11,760
making American toys, kids having fun, and parents having jobs.

469
00:34:14,300 --> 00:34:16,600
However simple or complex they are,

470
00:34:16,601 --> 00:34:19,740
these miniature playthings will inspire the next generation

471
00:34:19,741 --> 00:34:24,960
of American inventors, builders, and craftsmen.

472
00:34:24,961 --> 00:34:27,340
When you can make things, you can do anything.

473
00:34:27,341 --> 00:34:29,640
And manufacturing things that people love

474
00:34:29,641 --> 00:34:32,900
in the United States says to me that there's quality,

475
00:34:32,901 --> 00:34:35,240
there's innovation, and there's opportunity.

476
00:34:35,241 --> 00:34:36,920
And it's that kind of destiny that America

477
00:34:36,921 --> 00:34:38,320
