487
00:35:32,641 --> 00:35:40,640
The official flag of the United States has become one of the most recognizable symbols in the world.

488
00:35:43,640 --> 00:35:44,895
Take a look around.

489
00:35:44,896 --> 00:35:50,640
It's everywhere, adorning public buildings, doorsteps, and lining neighborhood streets.

490
00:35:50,641 --> 00:35:56,680
streets. The American flag is one product that demands to be made by domestic hands.

491
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:04,620
Annan Flag Makers in South Boston, Virginia, is one of the oldest and largest flag manufacturers

492
00:36:04,621 --> 00:36:05,340
in the world.

493
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:16,668
I ship probably pretty close to 18 to 20,000 flags a week, but I ship U.S.

494
00:36:16,669 --> 00:36:17,860
flags, I ship

495
00:36:17,861 --> 00:36:21,300
foreign country flags, I ship a lot of custom flags.

496
00:36:21,301 --> 00:36:23,860
We produce more U.S. than we do anything else.

497
00:36:26,660 --> 00:36:29,500
The U.S. flag-making business has come a long way

498
00:36:29,501 --> 00:36:33,180
since the days of Betsy Ross and Mary Pickersgill.

499
00:36:33,181 --> 00:36:35,820
Both considered pioneers in the art of flag-making

500
00:36:35,821 --> 00:36:39,620
in the late 17 and early 1800s.

501
00:36:39,621 --> 00:36:44,060
Back then, it would take a month to make one 30-by-40-foot flag.

502
00:36:44,061 --> 00:36:53,600
Today, that same flag can be made in just a few hours.

503
00:36:53,601 --> 00:36:59,520
The process begins with the arrival of the raw material, or gray goods, which are rolls

504
00:36:59,521 --> 00:37:03,360
of nylon and polyester.

505
00:37:03,361 --> 00:37:08,560
The material needs to first go through the dyeing process to convert the dull fabric

506
00:37:08,561 --> 00:37:11,540
into the flag's signature colors.

507
00:37:11,541 --> 00:37:17,160
We call these jig dyers, and once we put the material into the dyer, then it runs back

508
00:37:17,161 --> 00:37:19,300
and forth on rollers the whole length.

509
00:37:19,301 --> 00:37:22,660
There's a 3,000-yard roll in there, and it's running back and forth, running through the

510
00:37:22,661 --> 00:37:24,500
die at the bottom of the machine.

511
00:37:24,501 --> 00:37:28,160
From the time we put it in to the time we take it out, it takes us about 10 hours to

512
00:37:28,161 --> 00:37:32,780
die one 3,000-yard roll.

513
00:37:32,781 --> 00:37:39,540
In 1777, the Second Continental Congress passed the First Flag Act that ordered the

514
00:37:39,541 --> 00:37:41,840
to hold stripes of red and white,

515
00:37:41,940 --> 00:37:45,180
and the base of the star field to be blue.

516
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:51,780
These three colors symbolize courage, purity, and justice.

517
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:54,480
Once the dye process is completed,

518
00:37:54,580 --> 00:37:57,000
the rolls are to be cut into cakes,

519
00:37:57,100 --> 00:38:01,100
which will allow the three colors to be sewn together.

520
00:38:01,200 --> 00:38:04,000
These are all automatic sewing machines.

521
00:38:04,100 --> 00:38:06,940
When they load the stripes on, then the machines

522
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:08,800
will sit there and sew without an operator

523
00:38:08,801 --> 00:38:11,800
actually running the machine.

524
00:38:11,801 --> 00:38:13,800
When the bobbin runs out, they have to put a new bobbin thread in.

525
00:38:13,801 --> 00:38:16,800
If they break a thread, they have to keep up with that.

526
00:38:16,801 --> 00:38:21,800
And one operator usually runs about four machines.

527
00:38:21,801 --> 00:38:23,800
After leaving the automatics department,

528
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:28,800
the sewn stripes are cut into shorts or longs.

529
00:38:28,801 --> 00:38:32,800
The shorts are attached next to the embroidered star field,

530
00:38:32,801 --> 00:38:37,800
and the longs go underneath.

531
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:44,040
The fly hem is then added to prevent the flag from unraveling and shredding in the wind.

532
00:38:44,820 --> 00:38:49,620
A golden yellow fringe is added to those intended for interior settings.

533
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:54,660
The canvas heading is attached.

534
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:02,280
The brass grommets are inserted.

535
00:39:04,160 --> 00:39:07,080
And the flag is folded and boxed for shipment.

536
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:18,800
Annan has a rich background in providing flags to some of the most profound moments in United

537
00:39:18,801 --> 00:39:19,800
States history.

538
00:39:19,801 --> 00:39:24,800
We've been making flags for better than 165 years.

539
00:39:24,801 --> 00:39:28,800
We made the flag that was hoisted over Iwo Jima.

540
00:39:28,801 --> 00:39:32,800
We made the flag that was on Abraham Lincoln's coffin.

541
00:39:32,801 --> 00:39:37,800
We made the flag that was posted on the moon.

542
00:39:37,801 --> 00:39:42,800
Since Zachary Taylor took the presidential oath in 1849,

543
00:39:42,801 --> 00:39:46,800
Annan and Company has provided U.S. flags

544
00:39:46,801 --> 00:39:51,800
for every inauguration over the last 160 years.

545
00:39:51,801 --> 00:39:56,800
Well, we make American flags all the way from 4-by-6-inch stick flags

546
00:39:56,801 --> 00:40:01,800
that people wave on a stick all the way up through 30-foot-by-60-foot.

547
00:40:01,801 --> 00:40:05,800
The proportions of the flag were not officially standardized

548
00:40:05,801 --> 00:40:09,800
officially standardized until President William H. Taft

549
00:40:09,801 --> 00:40:14,800
signed the Executive Order of 1912.

550
00:40:14,801 --> 00:40:19,240
It prescribed the hoist and fly of every flag purchased

551
00:40:19,241 --> 00:40:24,900
for the government shall be a ratio of 10 to 19.

552
00:40:24,901 --> 00:40:29,560
Each year, this facility ships out over 500,000 flags

553
00:40:29,561 --> 00:40:31,660
to vendors all over the country.

554
00:40:31,661 --> 00:40:33,700
Along with the stars and stripes,

555
00:40:33,701 --> 00:40:36,120
Annan manufactures every state flag in the Union

556
00:40:36,121 --> 00:40:38,860
and every country flag in the United Nations.

557
00:40:39,660 --> 00:40:43,040
However, not all Annan flags are stitched and embroidered.

558
00:40:43,880 --> 00:40:45,140
Some are printed.

559
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:48,340
Today, Annan is screen printing what many consider

560
00:40:48,341 --> 00:40:50,220
to be its crowning achievement,

561
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,920
the POW MIA flag.

562
00:40:55,460 --> 00:40:57,700
During the height of the Vietnam War,

563
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:00,960
Annan flag makers was commissioned to create a flag

564
00:41:00,961 --> 00:41:04,580
that honored prisoners of war and those missing in action.

565
00:41:05,740 --> 00:41:09,980
In 1971, the black and white motif was unveiled

566
00:41:09,981 --> 00:41:12,600
and has since become the iconic image

567
00:41:12,601 --> 00:41:15,340
for those who have not yet come home from war.

568
00:41:17,060 --> 00:41:21,420
To this day, it is the only flag ever flown over the White House,

569
00:41:22,020 --> 00:41:23,880
alongside the stars and stripes.

570
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:28,620
The process begins with a scoured fabric

571
00:41:28,621 --> 00:41:31,900
that is adhered to a belt and fed through the line.

572
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:37,640
The printer will then dispense the liquid dye

573
00:41:37,641 --> 00:41:39,140
onto the inkwell of the screen.

574
00:41:41,020 --> 00:41:42,880
The platform will then drop,

575
00:41:43,540 --> 00:41:45,520
allowing for a magnet underneath the belt

576
00:41:45,521 --> 00:41:49,080
to propel a stainless steel rod across the screen,

577
00:41:50,780 --> 00:41:53,060
forcing the liquid dye through its pores.

578
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:56,760
This process is repeated

579
00:41:56,761 --> 00:42:00,200
until the color is completely deposited into the fabric.

580
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:03,600
Once the flags are printed,

581
00:42:04,180 --> 00:42:06,000
they will advance to the end of the belt

582
00:42:06,001 --> 00:42:08,180
where the wet ink is dried.

583
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:12,420
The material travels to the three-bowl washer

584
00:42:12,421 --> 00:42:15,680
to eliminate any excess or residual ink.

585
00:42:17,600 --> 00:42:20,700
Then it's straightened and dried.

586
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:33,440
From there, the flags are rolled, cut, and ready to be shipped out to vendors across the country.

587
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:39,860
With a large number of flags made under one roof,

588
00:42:40,980 --> 00:42:45,300
it's no wonder that Annan is one of the largest flag manufacturers in the world,

589
00:42:46,620 --> 00:42:49,920
and all of it made right here in the United States.

590
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:55,040
Annan prides itself on all of its product being U.S. made.

591
00:42:55,041 --> 00:42:58,200
We advertise all of our product as U.S. made.

592
00:42:58,580 --> 00:43:00,780
By rights, it should be made in the U.S.A.

593
00:43:04,180 --> 00:43:09,440
Today, being made in America invokes a new sense of pride for this country,

594
00:43:09,940 --> 00:43:16,620
a collaboration of man and machine that continues to push American innovation forward,

595
00:43:16,621 --> 00:43:24,820
led by an assembly line of fabricators, engineers, and artists.

596
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:29,640
who are filling the shelves with an array of homegrown products,

597
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:36,540
carrying on the manufacturing legacy that is made in the USA.

